  "metric_reconciliation_notes": {
    "prioritization_dataset_reconciliation": "In previous reports, the top project changed from EX-CDMO-201 (87% stability) to PRJ-001 (100% stability) because the evaluation switched from the 10-project conflicting Example Biologics Site portfolio to a 4-project illustrative dataset where PRJ-001 strictly dominated on all 5 criteria simultaneously (Penalty $75k, Tier 1A, Float 0.5d, Dependencies 4, Patient Impact True). In this release, both scenarios are evaluated and reported explicitly: the dominant scenario (trivially 100% stability) and the contrasting conflicting scenario (where criteria trade off and top stability varies from 72% at alpha0=10 to 98.6% at alpha0=100).",
    "peak_skid_utilization_reconciliation": "Defined standardized peak weekly skid utilization as max_{w in {W1, W2}} (hours on skid in week w / weekly capacity) * 100%. Capacity basis: nominal staffed weekly hours (120h UPLC, 100h Maurice, 90h Bioassay). Physical 24/7 calendar capacity is 168h/week. Utilization exceeding 100% in a feasible (no double-booking) schedule represents scheduled overtime/weekend load beyond nominal staffed capacity. Weighted tardiness units: dollars * days ($ * d).",
    "optimizer_claims_reconciliation": "When fixed work is strictly pinned across all methods, 100% fixed commitment protection is enforced for all methods. CP-SAT matches a strong earliest-due-date (EDD) dispatch rule on tardiness, and provides explainable schedule move reasoning traces and provable infeasibility diagnostics rather than superior capacity leveling.",
    "turnaround_forecaster_reconciliation": "At q50, pinball loss equals half of MAE. At q50 point prediction, the last-observed baseline achieves pinball loss 0.660 vs model 0.688. Paired bootstrap difference CI confirms model and last-observed baseline are statistically tied on point MAE and q50 pinball loss, while model strongly beats naive mean and project median.",
    "schedule_calibration_reconciliation": "Evaluated against an independent stress simulator with unmodeled Weibull machine wear-out and preemption across 100 held-out test scenarios. Agreement with the independent simulator is necessary but not sufficient evidence of real-world validity. Isotonic recalibration improves Brier score modestly from 0.1056 to 0.1040, but 95% cluster bootstrap CIs overlap."
  },
